    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.clue\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nA real-world example is with `dap.continue()`. Suppose we have `<leader>dc` postkeys `<leader>d`. When this command executes for the first time, it opens `vim.ui.select` to select the launch task. Then it types `<leader>d`, which is correct when `vim.ui.select` is not opened but incorrect when `vim.ui.select` is opened. Ideally if the `<leader>d` is not going to be caught by `mini.clue` it should not send it at all. In other words, the `postkeys` should only set the `mini.clue` prefix but not actually send the keys to Neovim.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nnightly a76f5f2ff\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n`<leader>12` will produce the issue with the following config (uncomment rtp lines to the appropriate directories):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.g.mapleader = \" \"\r\nvim.g.maplocalleader = \" \"\r\n\r\n-- vim.opt.rtp:prepend(vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/lazy/mini.clue\")\r\n-- vim.opt.rtp:prepend(vim.fn.stdpath(\"data\") .. \"/lazy/dressing.nvim\")\r\nrequire('mini.clue').setup({\r\n  triggers = {\r\n    { mode = 'n', keys = '<leader>' },\r\n    { mode = 'x', keys = '<leader>' },\r\n  },\r\n  clues = {\r\n    { mode = \"n\", keys = \"<leader>12\", postkeys = \"<leader>1\" },\r\n  },\r\n  window = { delay = 0 },\r\n})\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>12\", function() vim.ui.select({ 'a', 'b' }, {}, function() end) end)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nNo \"1\" inputted\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n\"1\" inputted",
