            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThat is a tough one. The reason why postkeys are directly emulated as key presses [is because it is hard to force exact order they are executed otherwise](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/92e2ae609f612f11f7e8e45d13614fcdff9f89b9/lua/mini/clue.lua#L1414-L1416). I remember trying really hard to make it work so that postkeys are just registered inside 'mini.clue' key query process, but didn't find a way to do that.\r\n\r\nThe main problem here is `vim.ui.select()` itself. Its implementation usually relies on user sending selection keys to it, but 'mini.clue' itself expects to intercept it in order to advance the key query process. So even if the first `<Space>12` shows select input and `<Space>1` is not sent to the Neovim, the next `2` should be processed by the 'vim.ui.select()` and not 'mini.clue'. Otherwise it will send `<Space>12` to the Neovim while select window is still open (as it didn't receive any keys).\r\n\r\nSo at the moment I *think* that this use case just doesn't fit in the 'mini.clue' model. I'll revisit this some time later, but there doesn't seem to be a good solution here.",
